      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "Follow these strict rules when generating code: do not use loops or arrays, do not use function parameters, and absolutely avoid all logical operators including NOT (!), AND (&&), and OR (||). All conditional logic must be written using strictly nested if/else statements; do not use else if chains. Use explicit boolean comparisons (e.g., if (conditionA === true)). Place all logic exclusively inside the existing updateAppUI arrow function, evaluating only the provided global variables conditionA and conditionB. The logic paths, text messages, and background colors must be based entirely and exactly on the flowchart or prompt provided by the student. Update the UI directly inside the nested blocks by assigning values to notificationMessage.innerText, notificationBackground.style.backgroundColor, and notificationBackground.style.color. Do not use CSS class toggling (e.g., classList.add). Completely ignore lab-overlay.js and any HTML/CSS associated with the testing lab overlay; do not generate or modify any code related to it. You must write the complete updateAppUI function covering all four possible outcomes explicitly; do not provide a partial implementation or leave placeholders."
      }
    },
    "display_name": "Streamer Alert Decisions",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Use your flowchart to code the logic for stream alerts.",
    "long_instructions": "### **Code the Streamer Alert System**\r\n\r\nYour **script.js** file has the variables ready, but the `updateAppUI()` function is empty. Let's use your flowchart to have the AI write the nested logic!\r\n\r\n#### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Prompt AI to generate the code using the flowchart saved in your Backpack.\r\n\r\n   *Example Prompt:*\r\n   > \"Use my flowchart to write a nested if/else statement inside updateAppUI(). Map my two questions to conditionA and conditionB. For all 4 outcomes, update notificationMessage.innerText and the background colors for notificationBackground.\"\r\n   \r\n2. Use the **conditionA** and **conditionB** toggles to test all four paths from your Test Cases table and verify the correct messages and colors appear.\r\n\r\n3. If the outcomes don't perfectly match your plan, debug it yourself or reprompt the AI to fix the mistakes.\r\n\r\n"
  },
